---
system: sys-14-retention-deletion-backup
flow_id: transcript-redaction-cron
surface: cron
spec_anchor: /software/systems/14-data-retention-deletion-backup#transcript-redaction-job
actors: [EventBridge, RetentionWorker, PostgreSQL, CloudWatch]
apis: []
externals: [EventBridge, CloudWatch]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - job_runs_constraint_violation
  - batch_lock_contention
  - partial_status_max_iterations
  - worker_crash_mid_batch
idempotency: redact only WHERE transcript_text != '[redacted]'; replay is no-op
retry: SKIP LOCKED prevents deadlock; next hourly run picks up missed rows
timeout: 5m soft (100 iterations × ~3s each); EventBridge no retry on hourly trigger
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Most legally sensitive retention job — 24h COPPA exposure window. Replaces seed-1 narrowly scoped to transcript redaction.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant EventBridge
    participant RetentionWorker
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant CloudWatch

    EventBridge->>RetentionWorker: rate(1 hour) trigger (transcript_redaction)
    RetentionWorker->>PostgreSQL: INSERT retention_job_runs (id, job_name='transcript_redaction', started_at=NOW(), status='running')

    alt job_runs_constraint_violation
        PostgreSQL-->>RetentionWorker: PK collision / NOT NULL violation
        RetentionWorker-->>EventBridge: error (worker exits non-zero)
        Note over RetentionWorker,CloudWatch: P1 alert — no redaction this hour
    else accepted
        PostgreSQL-->>RetentionWorker: ok

        loop iteration 1..100 (or until batch < 1000)
            alt batch_lock_contention
                RetentionWorker->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE session_turns SET transcript_text='[redacted]', response_text='[redacted]' WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM session_turns WHERE created_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours' AND transcript_text != '[redacted]' LIMIT 1000 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING id
                PostgreSQL-->>RetentionWorker: 0 rows (all locked by concurrent writer)
                Note over RetentionWorker: skip — next iteration will retry
            else rows_redacted
                PostgreSQL-->>RetentionWorker: N rows returned
                RetentionWorker->>RetentionWorker: yield 100ms between batches
            end
        end

        alt worker_crash_mid_batch
            RetentionWorker--xPostgreSQL: connection lost
            Note over PostgreSQL: row-level locks released — next hour run resumes
        else partial_status_max_iterations
            Note over RetentionWorker: 100 iterations exhausted — mark status='partial'
            RetentionWorker->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE retention_job_runs SET completed_at=NOW(), status='partial', rows_affected, iterations=100
        else completed
            RetentionWorker->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE retention_job_runs SET completed_at=NOW(), status='completed', rows_affected, iterations
        end

        RetentionWorker->>CloudWatch: emit retention_job_duration_ms, retention_rows_deleted (job_name=transcript_redaction)
    end

    Note over EventBridge,CloudWatch: 24h COPPA redaction window — idempotent via != '[redacted]' guard — alert if rows_affected=0 for 3 consecutive hours (potential silent failure)
